  "final_answer_preview": "Grievous hurt is specifically defined in the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, as any hurt that endangers life or causes the sufferer to experience severe bodily pain for a duration of fifteen days, or renders them unable to follow their ordinary pursuits. This definition is found in Section 116(h). Additionally, a person is said to voluntarily cause grievous hurt if they intend to cause grievous hurt and actually cause it, as outlined in Section 117(1). The explanation further clarifies that a person can still be considered to have voluntarily caused grievous hurt even if they intended to cause a different kind of grievous hurt but ended up causing another kind instead.",
